# Domain schema

Adding a vertical is a schema and data problem. It is not a core table change.

Do **not** add MTG, jewelry, tools, clothing, or any other domain fields to `Asset`, `Location`, `Container`, or `AssetType`.

```text
❌ Asset.mtgSet / foil / material / carat / serialNumber / shoeSize
✅ AssetType + attribute definitions/values (or Metadata until those tables persist)
✅ ExternalIdentifier (source + id) for Scryfall, Wikidata, …
✅ Controlled values with canonical keys (material.gold.14k), not alias strings
```

Core Asset may hold identity, type, name, notes, quantity, location/container, timestamps. Photos, tags, and history stay separate entities.

Follow [docs/taxonomy.md](docs/taxonomy.md). Do not build schema-driven forms, taxonomy import, or domain packs during the iOS UX pass ([docs/mobile-ux.md](docs/mobile-ux.md)).
